# Local secrets (API keys). Copy .env.example to .env -- .env is never committed.
/.env

# Eval campaigns (nesyplan/eval.py). Run artifacts, regenerated by
# scripts/run_experiment.sh -- so the heavy ones stay out of the repository.
#
# The exception is the shipped campaign's three TEXT artifacts: they are what
# docs/EXPERIMENT.md cites, and a claim whose evidence is not in the repository is
# not checkable. report.html (~9 MB) and the per-run PNGs/transcripts stay ignored;
# re-generate them by re-running the campaign.
/results/*
!/results/harness/
/results/harness/*
!/results/harness/manifest.json
!/results/harness/results.jsonl
!/results/harness/summary.md

# Session transcripts written by the demonstrators.
#
# The exception is replay_seed/: one recorded session committed on purpose, so
# `./scripts/run_web_demo.sh replay` works from a fresh clone with no API key. Your
# own recordings land elsewhere under llm_logs/ and take precedence (the picker
# prefers the newest usable one).
/llm_logs/*
!/llm_logs/replay_seed/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# macOS (AppleDouble siblings appear on ExFAT volumes) and editor cruft
._*
.DS_Store
*.swp
